comments.body:
This should purely be a mechanism for Tool authors to use the IsError field of the CallToolResult schema. It should only be used if the failure is something the Tool author wants returned to the LLM and not for internal errors.

```json
{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 2,
  "result": {
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "The document could not be found."
      }
    ],
    "isError": true
  }
}
```

Could be achieved through:

```csharp
throw new McpToolException("The document could not be found.");
```

Throwing any other exception would make the server return the usual error depending on the exception thrown:

```
{
  jsonrpc: "2.0";
  id: string | number;
  result?: {
    [key: string]: unknown;
  }
  error?: {
    code: number;
    message: string;
    data?: unknown;
  }
}
```

Which the client then handles in an implementation specific manner (as the client might have any implementation of MCP).

So this is a mechanism to return tool error results without failing at a protocol level.
